    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #341\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed branch `bb/relay-136-heartbeat-agent-tools-03-04-trigger-ti-thr_2uhea7yabj` to origin.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements `heartbeat.trigger({heartbeatId})` for issue #136, scoped identically to `heartbeat.list`/`heartbeat.history` (#135):\n\n- **`heartbeatAgentTools.ts`**: new `createHeartbeatTriggerTool` — validates ownership via `getHeartbeatForProject`, enqueues the existing `heartbeatFire` job with `{heartbeatId, triggeredByRunId}` for time-based rules (`dailyTime`, `weekly`, `interval`, `everyNDays`), and returns the canonical `heartbeat_event_triggered` error with no side effects for `onItemEvent` rules.\n- **`schedulerStore.ts`**: new `manualHeartbeatFireJobKey` (`heartbeat-fire:manual:${heartbeatId}`), distinct from the scheduler's own `heartbeatFireJobKey`, so pending scheduled and manual fires never collapse onto or overwrite each other, while repeated pending manual triggers do collapse onto one job.\n- **`sweep.ts`** / **`actions.ts`**: the fire task now threads an optional `triggeredByRunId` from the job payload into `ActionContext`, and `coreAgentRunAction` writes it as the new run's `parent_run_id` — child run history identifies the invoking parent.\n- **`schemaCoreModuleManifest.ts`**: registers `heartbeat.trigger` with the same \"no capability/approval gate\" terms as the other two tools.\n- Manual triggers never touch `next_fire_at`/`last_fired_at` (verified by test).\n\n## Test plan\n\n- Full backend build (all 11 packages) — clean.\n- `pnpm run test` (unit + integration + e2e) — 90/90, 669/669, 5/5 all passing.\n- `pnpm run lint` — clean.\n- `pnpm run check:boundaries` — no violations.\n- New/updated tests cover: dedup-key distinctness, manual-trigger job collapsing, non-collapse against a pending scheduled fire, the 409 `heartbeat_event_triggered` response with no enqueue, cross-project/unknown-id indistinguishability, and end-to-end `parent_run_id` attribution through the real queue.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
